---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const cli = 'https://github.com/nicodes/ghenv';
const actions = 'https://github.com/nicodes/ghenv-actions';
const command = [
	'ghenv run --clean-env \\',
	'  --repo OWNER/PROJECT \\',
	'  --secrets API_KEY \\',
	'  --vars API_BASE_URL \\',
	'  -- npm run dev',
].join('\n');
---

<Layout>
  <header class="header wrap">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="ghenv home"><span aria-hidden="true">[↳]</span>ghenv<span class="wordmark-dot">.</span></a>
    <nav aria-label="Main">
      <a class="header-link" href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
      <a class="header-link" href={`${cli}#readme`}>Docs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="header-link nav-source" href={cli}>GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>GITHUB → LOCAL DEVELOPMENT</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Dev secrets.<br /><span class="hero-title-accent">Delivered locally.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-description">Give your local command the development credentials it needs, straight from GitHub Actions. An encrypted handoff into its process environment. No local <code>.env</code> file.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="#get-started">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href={cli}>Explore the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-platform">GO CLI <span> / </span> LINUX + MACOS <span> / </span> YOUR GITHUB LOGIN</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="handoff" aria-labelledby="handoff-caption">
        <div class="preview-source">
          <div class="source-heading"><span class="tiny-label">01 / GITHUB ACTIONS</span><span class="scope-tag">Preview</span></div>
          <div class="source-title"><span class="source-icon" aria-hidden="true">{`{ }`}</span><div><strong>Your approved bundle</strong><span class="source-repository">OWNER/PROJECT</span></div></div>
          <div class="key-row"><code>API_KEY</code><span>••••••••••••</span><b aria-label="selected">↳</b></div>
          <div class="key-row"><code>API_BASE_URL</code><span>••••••••••••</span><b aria-label="selected">↳</b></div>
        </div>
        <div class="transfer"><span class="transfer-line" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="transfer-label"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 18" width="12" height="14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="7" width="12" height="9" rx="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M5 7V5a3 3 0 0 1 6 0v2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg> ENCRYPTED ARTIFACT</span><span class="transfer-line" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="transfer-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></div>
        <div class="terminal">
          <div class="terminal-bar"><span class="terminal-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>02 / YOUR MACHINE</span><span aria-hidden="true">↙</span></div>
          <div class="terminal-body"><p class="terminal-comment"># request only what you need</p><pre><code>{command}</code></pre><div class="terminal-result"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span><span>Selected values → child process</span></div></div>
        </div>
        <figcaption id="handoff-caption">Example handoff · your application runs locally.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <div class="principles wrap" aria-label="At a glance"><span><i aria-hidden="true">↳</i> Explicitly allowlisted</span><span><i aria-hidden="true">↳</i> Encrypted in transit</span><span><i aria-hidden="true">↳</i> Injected into the command</span></div>

    <section class="workflow section-space" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / THE HANDOFF</p><h2 id="workflow-title">A small round trip.<br />Then back to work.</h2><p>GitHub holds the approved development values. The CLI brings the selected ones to the command you’re about to run.</p></div>
        <ol class="flow-steps">
          <li><div class="step-top"><span>01</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><h3>Request by name</h3><p>The CLI creates a temporary key pair in memory and dispatches your repository’s <code>ghenv.yml</code> with its public key and requested names.</p><span class="step-detail">LOCAL → ACTIONS</span></li>
          <li><div class="step-top"><span>02</span><span aria-hidden="true">{`{ }`}</span></div><h3>Select. Encrypt. Upload.</h3><p>The action validates the Preview bundle, selects approved entries, and uploads an encrypted artifact. Application code needs no checkout.</p><span class="step-detail">AES-256-GCM + RSA-OAEP-SHA256</span></li>
          <li><div class="step-top"><span>03</span><span aria-hidden="true">↙</span></div><h3>Run on your machine</h3><p>The CLI downloads and decrypts in memory, attempts to delete the artifact, and starts your command with those values in its environment.</p><span class="step-detail">ACTIONS → LOCAL PROCESS</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="workflow-note">Each invocation waits for a GitHub runner and any required environment approval. Artifacts contain ciphertext and have one-day retention.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="setup wrap section-space" id="get-started" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
      <div class="setup-intro"><p class="eyebrow">02 / FIRST RUN</p><h2 id="setup-title">Wire it once.<br />Run your usual command.</h2><p>You’ll need Linux or macOS, Go 1.24+, the GitHub CLI, and a GitHub.com repository with Actions enabled.</p><div class="install-block"><p class="tiny-label">INSTALL + AUTHENTICATE</p><pre><code>{'go install github.com/nicodes/ghenv@latest\ngh auth login'}</code></pre></div><a class="text-link" href={`${cli}#setup`}>Full setup guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <ol class="setup-steps">
        <li><span class="setup-number">01</span><div><h3>Choose the development values</h3><p>Maintain a <code>GHENV_PREVIEW_BUNDLE</code> in your GitHub <code>Preview</code> environment, or explicitly assemble a bundle from existing Preview entries. The bundle is the complete export allowlist.</p><a href={`${actions}/blob/main/examples/ghenv-existing-preview.yml`}>Use existing Preview entries <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></li>
        <li><span class="setup-number">02</span><div><h3>Add the handoff workflow</h3><p>Copy the example to <code>.github/workflows/ghenv.yml</code> on your project’s default branch. Pin <code>ghenv-actions</code> to a reviewed full commit SHA and keep the job fixed to <code>Preview</code>.</p><a href={`${actions}/blob/main/examples/ghenv.yml`}>Open the workflow example <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></li>
        <li><span class="setup-number">03</span><div><h3>Launch your development command</h3><p>Request the exact secret and variable names your application reads. Put the command after <code>--</code>. GitHub authentication needs Actions read/write access.</p><pre class="run-command"><code>{command}</code></pre><p class="command-caption">Replace <code>OWNER/PROJECT</code> and the example names with your own.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="boundary section-space" aria-labelledby="boundary-title">
      <div class="wrap boundary-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / A DELIBERATE BOUNDARY</p><h2 id="boundary-title">You choose<br />what leaves GitHub.</h2><p>Only development credentials belong in the allowlist. Anyone permitted to dispatch and obtain required approval can request any entry in that bundle.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${cli}#export-boundary`}>Read the export boundary <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><dl class="boundary-list"><div><dt>Explicit Preview scope</dt><dd>The exporter checks version, environment, and repository. Production-marked bundles and requests outside the allowlist are rejected. Owners must ensure every selected value is a development credential.</dd></div><div><dt>A clean process environment</dt><dd><code>--clean-env</code> keeps terminal and tool paths while dropping unrelated inherited variables before injection. It also disables Expo dotenv loading. Remove other dotenv loaders from your launch command.</dd></div><div><dt>Local means locally readable</dt><dd>The application, local users, and administrators can inspect injected values. Keep keys developers must never read behind a remote API. Browser-facing settings remain public.</dd></div></dl></div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-section wrap section-space" aria-labelledby="details-title">
      <div class="details-heading"><p class="eyebrow">04 / GOOD TO KNOW</p><h2 id="details-title">A few practical details.</h2></div>
      <div class="questions">
        <details><summary>Already using individual Preview secrets?<span class="disclosure-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-body"><p class="faq-copy">The existing-Preview example assembles the bundle in memory from explicitly named secrets and variables. No duplicate credential secret is needed. Keep map keys and context references aligned, and ensure GitHub’s repository or organization fallback resolves to development values.</p><a class="faq-link" href={`${actions}/blob/main/examples/ghenv-existing-preview.yml`}>Existing Preview example ↗</a></div></details>
        <details><summary>What about private repos on GitHub Free?<span class="disclosure-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-body"><p class="faq-copy">Use the explicit repository development-bundle mode when environment secrets are unavailable. The bundle still has logical Preview scope, but this mode provides no GitHub environment approval protection. Reserve the bundle name for development values at every scope.</p><a class="faq-link" href={`${actions}/blob/main/examples/ghenv-repository-bundle.yml`}>Repository bundle example ↗</a></div></details>
        <details><summary>Can I run without credentials?<span class="disclosure-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-body"><p class="faq-copy"><code>ghenv local</code> applies the same environment isolation without GitHub authentication or an Actions round trip.</p><pre class="faq-command"><code>ghenv local -- npm run dev</code></pre></div></details>
        <details><summary>Does it replace every .env workflow?<span class="disclosure-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="faq-body"><p class="faq-copy">It replaces scalar settings when your app reads its process environment. Shell scripts that source dotenv files, Compose <code>env_file</code>, and tools requiring credential files need an adapter. Local database credentials and ports still need a local configuration source.</p><a class="faq-link" href={`${cli}#replacing-dotenv-files`}>Dotenv migration notes ↗</a></div></details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing wrap" aria-labelledby="closing-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">GITHUB → YOUR NEXT DEV SESSION</p><h2 id="closing-title">Bring your environment<br />to the command.</h2></div><div class="closing-actions"><a class="button" href={`${cli}#readme`}>Start with ghenv <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={actions}>Get the companion action <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  </main>
  <footer class="footer wrap"><a class="wordmark" href="/">ghenv<span class="wordmark-dot">.</span></a><span>Dev credentials. Local commands.</span><nav aria-label="Footer"><a class="footer-link" href={cli}>CLI source ↗</a><a class="footer-link" href={actions}>Action source ↗</a><a class="footer-link" href="https://www.ni.codes">By Nico ↗</a></nav></footer>
</Layout>
